- apps/web/src/components/threadActionMenu.logic.test.ts: the lifecycle-permission table runs three rows (mark-unread, mark-read, no read action) and asserts the single enabled read item, or none, without the operate permission.
- apps/web/src/hooks/useThreadActionMenu.test.ts and SidebarThreadRow.browser.test.tsx: fixtures follow the new hook export and row prop.
- Focused run of Sidebar.logic.test.ts, threadActionMenu.logic.test.ts and useThreadActionMenu.test.ts: 142 tests passed; Sidebar.browser.test.tsx and SidebarThreadRow.browser.test.tsx: 8 tests passed.
- Changed-files gate (node scripts/check-changed.ts HEAD, 12 files): format, lint, knip 1/2 and 2/2, typecheck of 2 packages, 264 tests in 13 files, the cross-file test run (7 tests) and the React compiler check on 7 files all passed; the gate over the follow-up's 7 files (196 tests in 8 files, the cross-file run with 4 tests, the React compiler check on 4 files) also passed.
- No test for the button's wiring, its pointerdown handling or its look, and no run in a real client.

